From: Mate Molnar <matemolnar88@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/wsi: 64-byte row alignment for CPU (wl_shm) images

Odd-width windows gave the swapchain blit an odd linear destination stride.
pvr then uses its "double stride" transfer, which locks up the GE8300
(SIPF v1; Fragment DM guilty lockup, fault address 0) as soon as a dialog
with an odd width opens. wl_shm accepts any stride, so align rows to 64 B.
---
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
@@ -3629,8 +3629,12 @@
       return result;
 
    if (chain->blit.type != WSI_SWAPCHAIN_NO_BLIT) {
+      /* 64-byte rows: keeps the blit destination stride an even number of
+       * pixels. pvr handles odd linear strides with a "double stride"
+       * transfer that hangs the GE8300 (SIPF v1); wl_shm takes any stride.
+       */
       wsi_configure_buffer_image(chain, pCreateInfo,
-                                 1 /* stride_align */,
+                                 64 /* stride_align */,
                                  1 /* size_align */,
                                  info);
 
